<article class="reference-container ats-guide policy-document">
<header class="ats-guide-intro"><span class="reference-eyebrow">PAYMENTS AND SERVICE REMEDIES</span><h1>Refund Policy</h1><p class="policy-status">Effective date: 16 October 2026</p><p>This policy covers digital CV building, analysis and document services purchased from <strong>Code Dev Solutions</strong> through <strong>atscvdetector.com</strong>. Email <a href="mailto:support@atscvdetector.com">support@atscvdetector.com</a> for payment or service questions.</p></header>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>1. Current payment status</h2><p>Available payment methods are shown at checkout. Registering, using welcome credits or viewing a plan does not authorise payment. Free services have no purchase price to refund. If you believe you were charged in our name, contact us with a transaction reference so we can investigate.</p><p>The provisions below apply to verified purchases. An unsuccessful AI request restores its reserved credits. A refunded credit purchase removes unused purchased credits; credits already spent may reduce the available balance.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>2. When to request a remedy</h2><p>Contact us for a duplicate charge, an unauthorised payment, a paid service not delivered, a technical failure preventing access to purchased output, or a service materially different from its description at purchase.</p><p>Where appropriate and legally permitted, we may first offer reasonable correction, repeat performance or restored access. If the problem cannot be fixed within a reasonable time, or the law gives an immediate refund right, we will provide the refund or other required remedy. Confirmed duplicate payments will be refunded in full. Unauthorised charges will be investigated alongside any payment-provider process.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>3. Request window</h2><p>For our voluntary service-problem review, contact us within <strong>14 calendar days</strong> of payment or discovery of a delivery problem, whichever is later. This helps investigation. It does not shorten any statutory complaint, cancellation, refund or payment-dispute period. Protected claims outside that window remain subject to applicable law.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>4. Outcomes and change of mind</h2><p>You purchase the described document service, not a job, interview, offer, salary or particular ATS score. Employer rejection, no employer response or a lower-than-expected estimate does not by itself establish a defective service.</p><p>We do not offer an automatic change-of-mind refund solely because a correctly described digital service has been completed or downloaded, except where law or purchase terms provide one. Downloading output, using AI or requesting immediate work does not automatically waive mandatory rights. Any legally valid consent required for immediate supply must be obtained separately.</p><p>Report errors, missing content or material delivery problems for assessment on their merits. This is not a blanket “all sales final” policy.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>5. Subscriptions</h2><p>Recurring plans disclose the billing period, renewal price, cancellation method and effective cancellation date before purchase. Cancelling future renewal and requesting a refund for a previous charge are separate actions. Statutory rights remain applicable. Registration alone is not recurring-billing consent.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>6. How to request help</h2><p>Email <a href="mailto:support@atscvdetector.com">support@atscvdetector.com</a> with “Refund request” in the subject. Include your account email, transaction reference, payment date and amount, a description of the issue and relevant screenshots. Redact unrelated information. Never send your password, PIN, full card number or security code.</p><p>We aim to acknowledge requests within five business days and give a decision or progress update within fourteen business days. If investigation takes longer, we will explain why. Legally required response periods take priority.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>7. Approved refunds</h2><p>Refunds normally return to the original payment method in the transaction currency, unless otherwise agreed or legally required. We aim to initiate an approved refund within ten business days, or sooner if required by law. Banks and payment providers may take additional time; we cannot guarantee their posting date. We do not deduct undisclosed refund administration fees.</p><p>Any partial refund for partial performance must be fairly explained and consistent with purchase terms and applicable law. A payment already reversed by a provider will not be reimbursed twice.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>8. Rights and complaints</h2><p>This policy supplements your rights. Contacting support does not require you to give up a bank dispute, regulatory complaint or court remedy. If you disagree with a decision, ask support for a review and provide further information. Where appropriate, contact the <a href="https://cpc.org.zw/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Consumer Protection Commission of Zimbabwe (opens in a new tab)</a> or another authority with jurisdiction.</p><p>Read this with our <a href="{{ route('terms') }}">Terms and Conditions</a> and <a href="{{ route('privacy') }}">Privacy Policy</a>. Revisions will not retrospectively remove rights attached to earlier purchases.</p></section>
